  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 01e979f63440fe7439b5b80889aceb94, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoPointController
  _resetTriggerTimeSeconds: 180
  _infoSign: {fileID: 845170301}
  _movePlayerToInfoPoint: 0
  _playerOrientation: {fileID: 1176295681}
  _infoPointHeadingText: Clinical Psychologist
  _subtitleText: Clinical psychologists are part of the care team in Clark Clinic.
    Our role with inpatients is to help support children and their families to cope
    with the experience of being in hospital and the many challenges this brings.
    This might be offering emotional support to parents while their child is awaiting
    surgery and helping them think about useful coping skills or how best to support
    siblings. It might be supporting and preparing children if they are anxious about
    procedures such as blood tests, cannulas or surgery. Or helping young people
    understand their heart condition and manage the demands of being unwell and in
    hospital, including if they are feeling worried or low in mood. Clinical psychology
    support is available to all inpatients during their stay in Clark Clinic. If
    you would like to speak with a clinical psychologist, please ask your nurse or
    doctor to make a referral for you, and we will arrange to meet with you as soon
    as we can.
  WaitingForCooldown: 0
